# Goal

Generation of the reference data using ASGARD-Legacy for the CI

# Strategy

The strategy is to compare a Sen2VM run (calling SXGEO beneath) versus an ASGARD-Legacy run (also calling SXGEO beneath)
Outputs are expected to be almost identical

## Step 1 - Set up environement

For the generation, all dependancies from Sen2VM are needed, and ASGARD-Legacy (with its dependencies), will also be needed.

An already well configured environment can be use, if so, please skip the first step

``` bash
# Step 1.1 - Base environment

## (Optional) Connect to a VM where everything asgard-build-env is available
ssh 172.26.45.33
## Or pull it looking at asgard documentation

## Launch a Docker to isolate the environment
docker run -it --rm --name asgard-legacy --user root --network host -v ~/.gitconfig:/root/.gitconfig2 -v ~/.m2:/root/.m2 -v /home/aburie/Sen2VM/:/home/aburie/Sen2VM -v $root_dir:$root_dir -v /DATA:/DATA -v /DATA-MPC2:/DATA-MPC2 -v /DATA-NETAPP-MPC:/DATA-NETAPP-MPC registry.eopf.copernicus.eu/geolib/asgard-build-environment bash

# Step 2.1 - Installation of ASGARD-Legacy
## Set-up GitLab tokens
export EOPF_PYPI_TOKEN= #TOKEN with access to GEOLIB and especially ASGARD-Legacy and asgard-legacy-drivers
export PIP_EXTRA_INDEX_URL="https://eopf:${EOPF_PYPI_TOKEN}@gitlab.eopf.copernicus.eu/api/v4/projects/14/packages/pypi/simple \
                     https://eopf:${EOPF_PYPI_TOKEN}@gitlab.eopf.copernicus.eu/api/v4/projects/67/packages/pypi/simple \
					 https://eopf:${EOPF_PYPI_TOKEN}@gitlab.eopf.copernicus.eu/api/v4/projects/92/packages/pypi/simple \
					 https://eopf:${EOPF_PYPI_TOKEN}@gitlab.eopf.copernicus.eu/api/v4/projects/171/packages/pypi/simple"

## Install ASGARD-Legacy and its dependencies.
## Use versions that are using the same SXGEO version than Sen2VM
pip install asgard_legacy==1.2.1
pip install asgard_legacy_drivers==0.1.1

## /!\/!\/!\ UNTIL ASGARD-LEGACY IS CORRECTED /!\/!\/!\
## ASGARD-Legacy is requiring direct location on integer, which is not a limitation in the code after

### EITHER  COPY FROM REPO:
cp <PATH_>/sen2vm-core/src/test/reference_generation/msi.py /usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/asgard_legacy/sensors/sentinel2/msi.py
### OR MODIFY IT DIRECTLY
 apt-get update
 apt-get install nano
 nano /usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/asgard_legacy/sensors/sentinel2/msi.py
  # TODO ======> remove line 552: 
  #     assert np.issubdtype(pixels.dtype, np.integer)


## Install additional dependencies for the reference generation script
pip install termcolor
pip install fiona
pip install rasterio
```

>[!IMPORTANT] A full already installed context is available on 172.26.45.33 with additional logs to better track from where differences could come

Instead of doing the previous commands, please only launch the other docker images

``` bash

## Connect to the VM where the docker image is available
ssh 172.26.45.33

# TODO: change the path to your home
docker run -it --rm -v  ~/.gitconfig:/root/.gitconfig2 -v ~/.m2:/root/.m2 -v /home/aburie:/home/aburie -v $root_dir:$root_dir -v /DATA:/DATA -v /DATA-MPC2:/DATA-MPC2 -v /DATA-NETAPP-MPC:/DATA-NETAPP-MPC ref_gen_sen2vm:v3 bash
```


## Step 2 - Generate grids with Sen2VM

First step is to generate the grids with Sen2VM. Indeed ASGARD-Legacy does not know on which point to perform direct/inverse locations. ASGARD-Legacy will only be used to verify the results of direct/inverse location, but not the generation of the grids which is handled in other CI tests.


``` bash
# The automatic tests can be launched with compilation command:
mvn clean install

# Outputs are generated inside folder: `sen2vm-core/src/test/resources/tests/output/`
```

## Step 3 - Generate grids with ASGARD-Legacy (using Sen2VM grids)

Sen2VM grids (generated through Step 2) then serve as inputs to generate references with ASGARD-Legacy.

The idea is to launch ASGARD-Legacy on each point of the grids and to save the ASGARD-Legacy results in new reference grids.

>[!WARNING] In the process, comparison is also performed between Sen2VM results and the ASGARD-Legacy results to anticipate any future CI failing once reference will be replaced.


``` bash
# Go inside script folder
# LOCATION IS IMPORTANT:
cd sen2vm-core/src/test/reference_generation
# Indeed, Sen2VM configuration file contains relativ path, so they are interpreted and paths are reconstructed within the script
# It is to be noted that if config.json file contains absolute path, you can launch the script from everywhere

# Remove outputs of previous run of the script
rm -Rf test_generation/*

# asgard-legacy-drivers is not robust to several GIPP in the same input folder
## Hence EITHER back-up input/data and rm them
cp -R sen2vm-core/src/test/resources/tests/data/ sen2vm-core/src/test/resources/tests/data_bk
rm sen2vm-core/src/test/resources/tests/data_bk/GIPP/S2A_OPER_GIP_BLINDP_MPC__20150605T094736_V20150622T000000_21000101T000000_B00.pdf
rm sen2vm-core/src/test/resources/tests/data_bk/GIPP/S2A_OPER_GIP_SPAMOD_MPC__20220120T000025_V20220125T022000_21000101T000000_B00.HDR
## Or rm them directly
# /!\/!\/!\ TO NOT PUSH THE SUPPRESSION, DO NO TO A git rm

# Example of launch command on the full reference folder
python3.11 test_legacy_sen2vm.py /home/aburie/Sen2VM/sen2vm-core/src/test/resources/tests/output/

# Outputs are generated in sen2vm-core/src/test/reference_generation/test_generation/
```


## Step 4 - Back-up ASGARD-Legacy grids as reference for Sen2VM


If previous step gave consitent grids between Sen2VM and ASGARD-Legacy

``` bash
# Go into the ref folder
cd sen2vm-core/src/test/resources/tests/ref/

# Remove previous reference data
rm -Rf */*

# Copy new reference data into the folders

for a in *; do cp -R ../../../reference_generation/test_generation/$a/* $a/ ; done
```


# Example of launch of the script on other data


## Launch on only on CI tests

* First perform Step 1 from above.

* Then perform step 2 of only run a chosen test with `mvn -Dtest=<test_file_withou_java_extention>#<test_name> test`

* Then launch the script:

``` bash
# Go in the ASGARD-Legacy script folder and clean previous runs
cd /home/aburie/Sen2VM/sen2vm-core/src/test/reference_generation/
rm -Rf test_generation/*

# Launch the script on previously run data
python3.11 test_legacy_sen2vm.py /home/aburie/Sen2VM/sen2vm-core/src/test/resources/tests/output/testDirectGipp/configuration.json /home/aburie/Sen2VM/sen2vm-core/src/test/resources/tests/output/testDirectGipp/params.json
python3.11 test_legacy_sen2vm.py /home/aburie/Sen2VM/sen2vm-core/src/test/resources/tests/output/testInverseLoc/configuration.json /home/aburie/Sen2VM/sen2vm-core/src/test/resources/tests/output/testInverseLoc/params.json
```

## Launch on personnal data

* First go in a working env (cf Step 1 above)

* Then create your data and launch the script:


``` bash
# Launch Sen2VM on some personal data
cd /home/aburie/Sen2VM/sen2vm-core/
#(Optional) Delete previous data from previous run
sudo rm -rf  /DATA/Sen2VM/MadeiraSAFE_SXGEO-0.3.1/S2B_MSIL1B_20241019T120219_N0511_R023_20241022T154709.SAFE/*/*/GEO*/
# Run Sen2VM
java -jar target/sen2vm-core-2.0.0-jar-with-dependencies.jar -c /DATA/Sen2VM/aburie/Sen2VM/MadeiraSAFE_SXGEO-0.3.1_configuration.json -p /DATA/Sen2VM/aburie/Sen2VM/params_B01_D01.json
# Grids are generated inside the product as it is a direct location configuration


# Go in the ASGARD-Legacy script folder and clean previous runs
cd /home/aburie/Sen2VM/sen2vm-core/src/test/reference_generation/
rm -Rf test_generation/*

# Launch the script on previously run data
python3.11 test_legacy_sen2vm.py /DATA/Sen2VM/aburie/Sen2VM/MadeiraSAFE_SXGEO-0.3.1_configuration.json /DATA/Sen2VM/aburie/Sen2VM/params_B01_D01.json
```